                        "content": "A client with severe acne is seen in the clinic, and the primary health care provider (PHCP) prescribes isotretinoin. The nurse reviews the client's medication record and would collaborate with the PHCP about the prescription if the client is also taking which medication?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nIsotretinoin is a metabolite of vitamin A and can produce generalized intensification of isotretinoin toxicity. Because of the potential for increased toxicity, vitamin A supplements should be discontinued before isotretinoin therapy. There are no contraindications associated with digoxin, phenytoin, or furosemide.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, the need to collaborate with the PHCP to ensure client safety. Recall that isotretinoin is a metabolite of vitamin A. Vitamin A is a fat-soluble vitamin; therefore, it is possible to develop toxic levels. This will direct you to the correct option.",
