                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nTopical glucocorticoids can be absorbed into the systemic circulation. Toxicity is a concern if a glucocorticoid is used for an extended period of time, if it is applied underneath an occlusive dressing, or if it is applied to a large area of the body. Therefore, options 1, 2, and 4 are incorrect.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, the potential for systemic absorption. Eliminate option 1 first by noting the time frame in the option. Next, eliminate option 2 by noting the size of the area. Choose option 3 over option 4 by noting the word occlusive in option 3.",
