                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nDoxycycline is a tetracycline. Adverse effects of isotretinoin can be increased by the use of tetracyclines. Tetracyclines increase the risk of pseudotumor cerebri and papilledema. Because of the potential for increased toxicity, tetracyclines need to be discontinued before isotretinoin therapy. Phenytoin, digoxin, and furosemide are not contraindicated.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nNote the subject, contraindications for use of isotretinoin. It is necessary to know the contraindications associated with the use of isotretinoin to answer this question. Remember that tetracycline is contraindicated with the use of isotretinoins.",
