                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nMupirocin is a topical antibacterial agent active against impetigo caused by staphylococci or streptococci. Cortisone would not be effective in treating impetigo. Benzoyl peroxide is a keratolytic. Acyclovir is a topical antiviral agent that inhibits DNA replication in the virus. It inhibits the activity of herpes simplex types 1 and 2, varicella zoster, Epstein-Barr virus, and cytomegalovirus.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, treatment for impetigo. Use knowledge of the pathophysiology of impetigo to answer correctly. Recall that an antibacterial is needed. Remember that mupirocin is used to treat impetigo.",
