                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nTransient leukopenia typically occurs after 2 to 3 days of treatment. Knowing this and knowing normal white blood cell values will direct you to option 3. Although options 1, 2, and 4 are abnormal findings, they are not associated with this medication.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, an adverse effect of 1% silver sulfadiazine. Specific knowledge of various burn treatments is needed to answer this question. Knowing that mafenide acetate (not silver sulfadiazine) has the adverse effect of metabolic acidosis will help you to eliminate option 4. Knowing that electrolyte imbalances can occur from the use of 0.5% silver nitrate (not silver sulfadiazine) will assist you in eliminating options 1 and 2.",
